ObICanBeatThat:

In Nethack 3.0j, I was on a quest to win with every character class; I
already had 4 or 5 down and I was starting to get careless (the game was
just too easy).  I got into the endgame with a Barbarian, and didn't 
notice that both my pickaxe and my holy water had been cursed in my
last encouter with the Wiz.  I wielded it to get through the maze and
I was stuck with it.  I was invisible, had a ring of conflict and a
ring of regeneration, so getting through the endgame was no problem; 
I just didn't fight anything.  But when I was going over the bridge to
the altar, the Wiz showed up again; I decided to just run for the altar.
When I was *1* space away, he stole the amulet and teleported away. 
I had to go hunt him down and pound on him with my pickaxe.  I still
had the ring of conflict and regeneration, plus about 200 HP, so he
couldn't hurt me as fast as I could heal, but it took forever to kill him,
and before he died I got Double Trouble, and the second Wiz stole the 
amulet from me again when I picked it up.  Before I could kill him,
he'd summoned another wiz, and I'd pretty much resigned myself to dying
here (the 2 wizards could slowly wear my HP down).  But then, when I was
down to about 40 HP, one of them summoned: a purple worm.  He swallowed
me so I could heal, but I still thought I'd never be able to kill the
Wizards.  Suddenly, I hear:

BURP!--More--
BURP!--More--

I kill the worm from inside and see no Wizards and one pile of stuff 
which included the real Amulet of Yendor.  Thanking the decomposing corpse
of the worm, I picked it up and went to win the game.
